```js
function loadSettings(readText) {
  return readText("settings")                 // promise of text.
    .then((text) => JSON.parse(text))          // throws on bad JSON, rejects the next promise.
    .then((settings) => {
      applyTheme(settings.theme);
      return settings;                         // passed down the chain.
    })
    .catch((error) => {
      showMessage("Settings were reset because they couldn't be read.");
      return { theme: "light" };               // recover with a default.
    });
}
```

| Inside a then handler | Next promise |
|---|---|
| return a value. | fulfils with that value. |
| return a promise. | waits for it, then follows it. |
| throw an error. | rejects with that error. |
| forget to return. | fulfils with undefined immediately. |

| After catch | Effect |
|---|---|
| catch returns a value. | chain recovers and continues fulfilled. |
| catch throws. | chain stays rejected. |

